## New components

### TitleCover

Stands in for a cover image: the title and the author set on a colored block, so the detail page has a visual anchor without uploads.

- Closest existing: Avatar, Card. Why not: Avatar draws initials in a circle of at most 56 px, and Card is a surface for content; neither sets a title in a 2:3 block.
- Look: A 160 by 240 block in the entity color that stands in for a cover: the title at the top in the heading size, up to four lines, and the author on one line at the bottom. Quiet and bookish, like a cloth binding; it is the visual anchor of the detail page, not a call to action.
- Width: 160 to 160. Box: 160 wide, 240 tall, padding 4, gap 2; column gap 2 padding 4 align stretch justify between.
  - [text] the book title, up to four lines: {Book.title} \`TitleCover.n01\`
  - [Truncate] the author on one line: {Book.author} \`TitleCover.n02\`
- Used on: S06.
"
